<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phan Bội Châu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1867–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Phan Boi Chau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phan Bội Châu was a Vietnamese nationalist and scholar who sought to free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> from French rule. He founded the Modernisation Society in 1904 and the Đông Du movement, which sent young Vietnamese to study in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and later formed a revolutionary league in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Seized by French agents in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> in 1925, he spent his last years under house arrest in Huế.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phan-boi-chau.jpg" alt="Phan Bội Châu" width="225" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phan_Boi_Chau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
